{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:25:04.743025Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f5126aca-4e8f-4496-aebc-7b47c7afcdbc","text":"Rewrote `spec.md` (not committed yet). It covers every Q\u0026A decision, tags each feature MVP/V2/V3, and ends with a proposed backlog of 28 items (§18).\n\n**Agent decisions not covered in the Q\u0026A:**\n- The library is a folder with one file per palette, so V3 sync needs no migration\n- `.colorsip` is DTCG JSON with metadata under `$extensions[\"app.colorsip\"]`\n- De-duplication uses ΔEOK \u003c 0.002\n- Picks are added to the end of the target palette's ungrouped section\n- Drag moves a swatch, Option-drag copies it\n- The MVP gets a compact editor sheet in the popover, because the main window doesn't arrive until V2\n- Smart Profiles use the app under the pointer, not the frontmost app\n- Contrast fix changes OKLCH lightness only\n- Color vision simulation uses the Machado 2009 matrices\n\nBacklog issues will be filed once the user approves."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:27:21.497964Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4acfd674-beaa-4072-98e0-31f086c39d88","text":"**Revision (user):** new picks go to the **front** of the target palette's ungrouped section, so the user doesn't have to scroll for every pick. Updated §4.5 and §7.1."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:30:06.552345Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-71a6c7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"MVP release. Scope: `spec.md` §2 (items 1–17 in §18).\n\nMenubar app, palettes with named groups, Color History, picker (single and multi pick, precise movement, Cmd+click paste), color profiles / Smart Profiles, global shortcut, settings, permissions onboarding.","labels":["epic"],"parent_id":"cs-54d4cf","sort_order":"a0","title":"MVP: menubar app, palettes, picker, color profiles"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:12.54229Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-db6fed","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"V2 release. Scope: `spec.md` §2 (items 18–25 in §18).\n\nMain window app, import/export, contrast checker (including the picker's contrast mode), color vision simulation.","labels":["epic"],"parent_id":"cs-54d4cf","sort_order":"a1","title":"V2: main window, import/export, contrast checker, color vision"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:13.852297Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-05f589","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"V3 release. Scope: `spec.md` §2 (items 26–28 in §18).\n\nSmart Formats, templates, file-system sync.","labels":["epic"],"parent_id":"cs-54d4cf","sort_order":"a2","title":"V3: Smart Formats, templates, file-system sync"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:14.866778Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-70c2c3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §1.\n\n- [ ] Xcode project, macOS 15.8+, Swift 6, agent app (`LSUIElement`, no Dock icon), not sandboxed\n- [ ] `ColorsipCore` Swift package (no UI) with Swift Testing set up\n- [ ] GitHub Actions: build the app and run the Core tests on push and PR\n- [ ] README: build from source, grant permissions\n- [ ] MIT `LICENSE`","labels":["task"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a3","title":"Project scaffold: agent app, ColorsipCore package, CI, README, MIT license"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:20.884756Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7375e5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-7375e5","target_id":"cs-70c2c3"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §5.1. Lives in ColorsipCore.\n\n- [ ] `Color` = color space + Float64 components + alpha (CSS Color 4 / DTCG model), no clamping or rounding when stored\n- [ ] Spaces: srgb, display-p3, generic-rgb, oklab, oklch, hsl, hwb, plus HSB for the editor\n- [ ] Conversions between all spaces (through linear light / XYZ)\n- [ ] ΔEOK equality (threshold 0.002) for de-duplication\n- [ ] CSS Color 4 gamut mapping to sRGB (OKLCH chroma reduction), and an sRGB `hex` fallback\n- [ ] Unit tests against reference values","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a4","title":"Color model, color spaces and conversions"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:28.243904Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-5cda46","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-5cda46","target_id":"cs-70c2c3"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §3.1.\n\n- [ ] Status-bar icon that opens a popover (popover can't be detached)\n- [ ] Toolbar: picker and new palette (V2 buttons hidden)\n- [ ] Format dropdown (placeholder until formatters land)\n- [ ] Bottom bar: Settings and Quit (V2 controls hidden)\n- [ ] Launch at login via `SMAppService`, off by default","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a5","title":"Menubar status item and popover shell"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:30.435641Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-86d22b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-86d22b","target_id":"cs-7375e5"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §5.3. Lives in ColorsipCore.\n\n- [ ] CSS Hex (with and without #, alpha as #rrggbbaa), CSS rgb(), hsl(), oklch(), color(display-p3 …)\n- [ ] SwiftUI Color, NSColor, UIColor, Android (0xAARRGGBB / #AARRGGBB)\n- [ ] Gamut-map to sRGB for formats that can't express the color's gamut\n- [ ] Unit tests for every format","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a6","title":"Output formatters"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:34.405326Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-06fad2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-06fad2","target_id":"cs-7375e5"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §5.5.\n\n- [ ] Bundle meodai/color-name-list (MIT), with license attribution\n- [ ] Nearest-name lookup by ΔEOK in OKLab, fast enough for live use in the loupe (precomputed index)\n- [ ] Unit tests","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a7","title":"Color naming with color-name-list"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:36.423851Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-39dff3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-39dff3","target_id":"cs-7375e5"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §5.2, §7, §11.\n\n- [ ] Model: library → palettes (name, description, icon, locked, timestamps) → ungrouped section plus groups (one level) → swatches\n- [ ] Rules: swatches unique within a group; locked palettes can't be changed; at most one pick target\n- [ ] Library folder layout (`library.json`, `history.json`, `settings.json`, `palettes/\u003cuuid\u003e.colorsip`), atomic writes\n- [ ] `.colorsip` as DTCG JSON with `$extensions[\"app.colorsip\"]` and `formatVersion`\n- [ ] JSON Schema 2020-12 at `schema/colorsip-palette.schema.json`, validated in tests\n- [ ] Undo/redo for all library changes","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a8","title":"Library model, on-disk storage, .colorsip DTCG format and undo"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:39.586522Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7f6ead","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-7f6ead","target_id":"cs-5cda46"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §4.1, §10.\n\n- [ ] Settings window with the General, Shortcuts, Picker, Profiles and Permissions panes (Profiles content comes from the Smart Profiles issue)\n- [ ] Global picker shortcut, default Hyper+P (Ctrl+Option+Cmd+P), user can change it, conflict feedback\n- [ ] Shortcut infrastructure ready for the optional V2 shortcuts (contrast checker, main window)\n- [ ] Synced settings stored in `settings.json`; machine-local state in UserDefaults","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"a9","title":"Settings window and global shortcuts"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:42.222173Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-0fb394","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-0fb394","target_id":"cs-5cda46"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §9.\n\n- [ ] Check for missing permissions at launch and whenever a feature needs one\n- [ ] Guide through missing permissions one at a time: explanation, a button that opens the right System Settings pane, live detection that moves on once granted\n- [ ] Accessibility can be skipped (only needed for Cmd+click paste)\n- [ ] Permission status and a \"start guide again\" button in Settings","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aA","title":"Permissions onboarding (Screen Recording, Accessibility)"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:44.393307Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-7f6ead","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"source_id":"cs-7f6ead","target_id":"cs-5cda46","kind":"blocked_by"},{"source_id":"cs-7f6ead","target_id":"cs-39dff3","kind":"blocked_by"}],"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:49.046968Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-a29255","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-a29255","target_id":"cs-39dff3"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-a29255","target_id":"cs-5cda46"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §3.1, §7.3.\n\n- [ ] Scrollable palette list in the popover: radio button, icon, name, lock icon, strip\n- [ ] Strip: equal-width segments sized so 16 fill the width; each group as its own rounded segment with a gap\n- [ ] Over 16 colors: horizontal scroll with faded edges where there's more content\n- [ ] Empty palette shows the dashed \"Drop colors here\" target\n- [ ] Click a swatch to copy its value in the active format; right-click for Copy as…","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aB","title":"Palette list and swatch strips"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:51.592926Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-40b6c9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-40b6c9","target_id":"cs-86d22b"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-40b6c9","target_id":"cs-06fad2"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-40b6c9","target_id":"cs-7f6ead"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-40b6c9","target_id":"cs-0fb394"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §4.1–4.3.\n\n- [ ] Open with the global shortcut or the toolbar eyedropper\n- [ ] Transparent overlay over every display; follows the pointer across displays with different scale factors and profiles\n- [ ] ScreenCaptureKit sampling in the native space of the display under the pointer\n- [ ] Circular loupe with a magnified pixel grid and the center pixel outlined\n- [ ] Mouse wheel changes the diameter (120–400 pt, default 200); Option + wheel changes the grid size (5–31, odd only, default 11); both remembered\n- [ ] Arrow keys move 1 physical pixel, Shift + arrow 10; Esc cancels\n- [ ] Label shows the value in the active format and the friendly name","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aC","title":"Picker overlay and loupe"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:54.910463Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-979715","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-979715","target_id":"cs-39dff3"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-979715","target_id":"cs-a29255"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §7.4.\n\n- [ ] Always first in the list; no radio button, no lock\n- [ ] Last 16 picks, newest first; re-picking an existing color moves it to the front\n- [ ] Read-only: can't be cleared, edited or reordered; users can copy from it and drag out of it (always a copy)\n- [ ] Stored in `history.json`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aD","title":"Color History"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:31:58.997101Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d6bd2c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-d6bd2c","target_id":"cs-a29255"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §3.1, §7.1, §7.2.\n\n- [ ] New palette (+); context menu: Rename, Edit description, Set icon, Lock/Unlock, New group, Duplicate, Delete\n- [ ] Icon picker: emoji or SF Symbol\n- [ ] Reorder palettes by dragging\n- [ ] Groups: create, rename, reorder, delete (ask whether to delete the swatches or move them to ungrouped)\n- [ ] Swatch context menu: Rename, Delete (hidden when locked)\n- [ ] Pick-target radio button (at most one palette); locked palettes can't be the target\n- [ ] Locked palettes only offer Unlock","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aE","title":"Palette and group management in the popover"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:01.71155Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-c07049","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-c07049","target_id":"cs-d6bd2c"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §7.5.\n\n- [ ] Drag between palettes and groups, and within a group to reorder; drag out of Color History\n- [ ] Plain drag moves, Option-drag copies, dragging from history always copies\n- [ ] Drop targets: palette strip, group header, the empty \"Drop colors here\" area\n- [ ] Refuse a duplicate in the same group and briefly highlight the existing swatch; refuse drops on locked palettes\n- [ ] Drag out to other apps: the value as text in the active format, plus an NSColor\n- [ ] Undoable","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aF","title":"Drag and drop of swatches"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:06.162733Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-722793","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-722793","target_id":"cs-86d22b"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-722793","target_id":"cs-d6bd2c"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §5.4.\n\n- [ ] Opens as a sheet from the popover (swatch → Edit…)\n- [ ] 2D saturation/brightness field, hue slider, alpha slider\n- [ ] Model switcher for numeric fields: HEX, RGB, HSB, HSL, OKLCH, Display P3; alpha in every model\n- [ ] Name and description fields; eyedropper button to re-pick; \"…\" menu with Copy as and Reset\n- [ ] Undoable; not available for locked palettes or Color History","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aG","title":"Compact color editor sheet"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:08.573198Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-995046","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-995046","target_id":"cs-979715"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-995046","target_id":"cs-d6bd2c"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-995046","target_id":"cs-40b6c9"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §4.3–4.5.\n\n- [ ] Single mode: click, Return or Space picks and closes\n- [ ] Shift+click picks and keeps the picker open\n- [ ] Multi mode: every click picks; Esc or Return without moving finishes, keeping the picks\n- [ ] Holding Option shows the mode popover menu (Single, Multi; Contrast hidden until V2)\n- [ ] Every pick goes into Color History, and to the **front** of the target palette's ungrouped section unless it's locked\n- [ ] The last pick's value is copied to the clipboard in the active format\n- [ ] Picks are auto-named and undoable (except their effect on history)","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aH","title":"Picker modes and pick routing"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:11.801121Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-901e7e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-901e7e","target_id":"cs-995046"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §4.5.\n\n- [ ] Remember which app was active before the picker opened\n- [ ] Cmd+click picks, closes the picker, re-activates that app, puts the value on the clipboard and sends a synthetic Cmd+V (CGEvent)\n- [ ] Without the Accessibility permission: only copy, and point the user to the onboarding step\n- [ ] Leave a hook for Smart Formats (V3) to choose the format per target app","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aI","title":"Cmd+click paste into the active app"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:15.607585Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-615265","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-615265","target_id":"cs-40b6c9"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-615265","target_id":"cs-7f6ead"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §6.\n\n- [ ] Find the app that owns the window under the pointer (not the frontmost app)\n- [ ] Convert the sampled value from the display's space to that app's target profile\n- [ ] Built-in mappings: browsers and Figma → sRGB; Xcode, Sketch, Pixelmator Pro, Preview → Display P3\n- [ ] Settings ▸ Profiles: add, edit and remove app → profile rows; fallback profile (Display native, sRGB, Display P3, Generic RGB; default sRGB)\n- [ ] The loupe label shows a badge with the profile it used","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-71a6c7","sort_order":"aJ","title":"Color profiles / Smart Profiles"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:18.502041Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-3ba60e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-3ba60e","target_id":"cs-71a6c7"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §3.2.\n\n- [ ] Opens from the popover's bottom bar and an optional global shortcut; still no Dock icon\n- [ ] Sidebar: Color History plus palettes with strips\n- [ ] Content: collapsible groups; rows with swatch, name and value; list/grid toggle; sort (manual, name, hue, lightness, date added); empty state\n- [ ] Inspector for a palette: name, description, info (created, modified, color count), Lock toggle\n- [ ] Bottom actions: Export, Duplicate, Delete\n- [ ] Toolbar: new palette, view toggle, sort, picker, contrast checker, color vision, format dropdown","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aK","title":"Main window: three panes, list/grid view, sort, inspector"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:21.223958Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-fa45b1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-fa45b1","target_id":"cs-3ba60e"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-fa45b1","target_id":"cs-722793"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §3.2, §5.4.\n\n- [ ] Reuse the compact editor in the main window inspector, with description and info (created, modified)\n- [ ] Several colors selected: \"Multiple Values\" mode, where differing fields show \"Multi\" and an edit applies to every selected color\n- [ ] Undoable as a single step","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aL","title":"Inspector color editor with multi-selection editing"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:25.90751Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-44570f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-44570f","target_id":"cs-39dff3"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §11.2, §12.\n\n- [ ] Exported UTI `app.colorsip.palette`, extension `.colorsip`\n- [ ] Export from the palette context menu, the inspector and File ▸ Export (locked palettes too)\n- [ ] Import from File ▸ Import, drag and drop, and double-clicking a file\n- [ ] Importing never overwrites: an id already in the library becomes a copy\n- [ ] Shared export plumbing for the other formats","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aM","title":"Import/export: Colorsip document type"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:28.313161Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-2544ad","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-2544ad","target_id":"cs-7375e5"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-2544ad","target_id":"cs-7f6ead"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §8.1.\n\n- [ ] Window with text and background colors, live \"Aa\" preview in several sizes, score\n- [ ] Algorithm switch: WCAG 2.x (ratio, AA/AAA for normal and large text) or APCA (Lc against a target)\n- [ ] Sliders and color fields on each side; real-time score\n- [ ] Fix buttons on both sides: smallest OKLCH lightness change on that side that meets the target; hue and chroma kept (gamut-mapped); target selectable (default WCAG AA normal / APCA Lc 60)\n- [ ] Opens from the toolbar button, an optional global shortcut, and \"Check contrast with…\" in the main window\n- [ ] Contrast math in ColorsipCore, with unit tests","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aN","title":"Contrast checker (WCAG 2.x and APCA, fix buttons)"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:31.715788Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-602bc4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-602bc4","target_id":"cs-a29255"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §8.2.\n\n- [ ] Modes: Off, Protanopia, Deuteranopia, Tritanopia, Achromatopsia\n- [ ] Changes only how swatches are drawn (popover and main window); stored and copied values stay the same\n- [ ] Machado et al. (2009) matrices at full severity, in linear sRGB; achromatopsia uses luminance\n- [ ] Opens from the toolbar color wheel and the bottom-bar menu; the current mode stays visible while it's on\n- [ ] Open question (spec §17): keep both menus, or just one?","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aO","title":"Color vision simulation"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:34.200981Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-86d9fe","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-86d9fe","target_id":"cs-44570f"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §12.\n\n- [ ] Adobe Swatch Exchange (`.ase`): groups map to ASE groups\n- [ ] Apple Color List (`.clr`): no groups, so names are flattened to \"Group / Name\"\n- [ ] JSON: `{ name, groups: [{ name, colors: [{ name, hex, rgba, oklch }] }] }`\n- [ ] Round-trip tests where a reader exists","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aP","title":"Export: ASE, CLR and JSON"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:39.270926Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-493cfd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-493cfd","target_id":"cs-44570f"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §12.\n\n- [ ] One page per palette; header with the palette name and description\n- [ ] Each group is a section; each swatch is a tile labeled with name, HEX, RGB and OKLCH\n- [ ] PDF tagged with the Display P3 profile\n- [ ] Open question (spec §17): paper size, light/dark background","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aQ","title":"Export: PDF"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:41.102848Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-81d6ee","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-81d6ee","target_id":"cs-2544ad"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-81d6ee","target_id":"cs-995046"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §4.4.\n\n- [ ] Add Contrast to the Option mode popover menu\n- [ ] Flow: pick the text color, then the background color, then the contrast checker opens with both\n- [ ] The loupe label says which of the two is being picked","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-db6fed","sort_order":"aR","title":"Picker contrast mode"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:43.165971Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-523d6a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-523d6a","target_id":"cs-86d22b"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-523d6a","target_id":"cs-7f6ead"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §13.\n\n- [ ] Settings ▸ Formats: assign an output format per app bundle ID\n- [ ] On copy, use the format of the app frontmost at copy time; when Colorsip is frontmost, the app that was active before it\n- [ ] Cmd+click paste uses the format of the app it pastes into\n- [ ] Apps without an assignment use the format dropdown's format\n- [ ] Optional: when the dropdown changes while app X was active, offer to assign that format to X","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-05f589","sort_order":"aS","title":"Smart Formats"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:45.581279Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-e84626","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-e84626","target_id":"cs-d6bd2c"},{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-e84626","target_id":"cs-995046"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §14.\n\n- [ ] Template = palette skeleton of groups with named, empty slots\n- [ ] Create a palette from a template; picking fills the next empty slot in order; the loupe label shows the slot name; clicking a slot makes it the next one\n- [ ] Built-in: Tailwind theme (slots 50–950, every shade picked by hand, nothing generated), Web UI, iOS/macOS/Android UI semantic roles\n- [ ] Save any palette with groups as a template (keeps groups and names, clears colors)\n- [ ] Open question (spec §17): exact Tailwind color groups","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-05f589","sort_order":"aT","title":"Templates: built-in templates, pick into slots, save as template"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:48.376988Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-d9d329","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocked_by","source_id":"cs-d9d329","target_id":"cs-39dff3"}],"description":"Spec: `spec.md` §15.\n\n- [ ] Settings ▸ Sync: choose a folder; the library moves into it\n- [ ] Everything syncs: palettes, Color History, library order, settings\n- [ ] On a fresh install, pointing at an existing sync folder brings everything back as it was\n- [ ] Watch the folder (FSEvents / NSFilePresenter) and reload changed files live\n- [ ] Conflicts resolved per file: newer `modifiedAt` wins; the losing version is kept as `\u003cuuid\u003e.conflict-\u003ctimestamp\u003e.colorsip` and shown to the user; detect provider-created conflicted copies","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"cs-05f589","sort_order":"aU","title":"File-system sync (Dropbox, OneDrive, Google Drive folders)"},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:32:50.901764Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"cs-f1a73a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5e2698cb-65db-4d72-9a56-639081769f2b","text":"**Backlog filed.** It has release epics MVP cs-71a6c7 (17 stories), V2 cs-db6fed (8) and V3 cs-05f589 (3), all under cs-54d4cf, with `blocked_by` links matching spec §18.\n\nSmall changes from the spec table:\n- Settings (cs-7f6ead) is also blocked by library storage (cs-39dff3), because it writes `settings.json`.\n- The main window (cs-3ba60e) is blocked by the MVP epic as a whole.\n\n§18 now points to the epic IDs. Waiting for user approval before committing."},"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:33:00.204619Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
